"cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && timeout 80 git pull -q 2>&1|tail -2; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | head -60"], ["timeout", "100000"]], "output": "```console\n084f3a7 Brief revision 6: decisions on CMP, adaptive HT, GNN, cluster HT\n76116b6 Brief revision 5: part (i) judged on the discriminating set D (heterogeneous degree, clusters, spec ladder, real graphs); cell budget and family counts\n0be35f3 Brief revision 4: P5 acceptance rule per target with null simulation, cell budget, edge-noise slice, DM bias per design, corner check, SNR\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n-# Brief — idea of the study (revision 5, after idea-review round 3)\n+# Brief — idea of the study (revision 6, after idea-review round 3 and experiment-repo#6)\n-- **Estimators and information tiers** (a comparison is only valid inside a tier): **Tier G (generic information)**: every estimator knows the graph and uses only generic exposure forms with no mechanism-specific parameter: DM; Hájek/HT with fraction-threshold exposure at fixed generic q (Aronow–Samii/Eckles et al.); cluster DM; Chin regression (own z + neighbour fraction); +count; +2-hop; +interaction. **Tier A (data-adaptive)**: specification/threshold/penalty chosen from the data by a protocol fixed in advance (cross-validation with dependence-respecting folds, e.g. graph-cluster folds with a buffer, plus a held-out-corner check defined as: for each exposure feature, fit on units below its q-th quantile (q = 0.7 fixed in advance) and score on units above it, where the held-out units mimic the extrapolation to the corner; selection uses the sum of the CV loss and the corner loss; identical for linear, ridge, trees/boosting, optional small GNN): Han–Ugander ReFeX-LASSO-style selection, HT with data-adaptive thresholds (Thiyageswaran et al. 2024), causal message-passing regression (Shirani & Bayati 2024) where runnable. **Tier O (oracle)**: correct feature form with and without known parameters (ρ, threshold) reported separately; the parameters-fitted version (nonlinear least squares) is the legitimate floor. Optional: Cortez et al. staggered rollout (own design), Yu et al. 2022 (unknown structure). The GNN arm runs on a subset of cells only and the paper says so.\n+- **Estimators and information tiers** (a comparison is only valid inside a tier): **Tier G (generic information)**: every estimator knows the graph and uses only generic exposure forms with no mechanism-specific parameter: DM; Hájek/HT with fraction-threshold exposure at fixed generic q (Aronow–Samii/Eckles et al.); cluster DM; Chin regression (own z + neighbour fraction); +count; +2-hop; +interaction. **Tier A (data-adaptive)**: specification/threshold/penalty chosen from the data by a protocol fixed in advance (cross-validation with dependence-respecting folds, e.g. graph-cluster folds with a buffer, plus a held-out-corner check defined as: for each exposure feature, fit on units below its q-th quantile (q = 0.7 fixed in advance) and score on units above it, where the held-out units mimic the extrapolation to the corner; selection uses the sum of the CV loss and the corner loss; identical for linear, ridge, trees/boosting, optional small GNN): Han–Ugander ReFeX-LASSO-style selection, HT with data-adaptive thresholds (Thiyageswaran et al. 2024) (the simplified adaptive-threshold Hájek, reported under that name; see the baseline decisions below). **Tier O (oracle)**: correct feature form with and without known parameters (ρ, threshold) reported separately; the parameters-fitted version (nonlinear least squares) is the legitimate floor. Optional: Cortez et al. staggered rollout (own design), Yu et al. 2022 (unknown structure). The GNN arm runs on a subset of cells only and the paper says so.\n+**Decisions on baselines that cannot be run as published (rev. 6, after `experiment-repo`#6).** (1) *Causal message passing (Shirani & Bayati 2024)* is defined for panel outcomes (several time steps on a fixed graph); the study has one outcome per unit at one assignment, so it is **dropped from the comparison**, and the text says why in one sentence. No different method is run under its name. The one-shot m\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "27c46873-8451-5256-a5e4-6f475b21401f", "at": 1795638792.6462085, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26729, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "07888da8ceffe85cd9b61d7e99abda5a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "72eb5c7a-4a0b-5523-85af-0b8f98d7e4c1", "at": 1795638792.6487398, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26730, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "07888da8ceffe85cd9b61d7e99abda5a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "605c952a-d234-596e-8051-f0ede9fbe5e8", "at": 1795638792.6507287, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26731, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "07888da8ceffe85cd9b61d7e99abda5a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "365897e7-04e8-5a52-95f9-32adafff8263", "at": 1795638793.6286914, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26732, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "07888da8ceffe85cd9b61d7e99abda5a", "trust": "system-confirmed